{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChLYnrUZnCLTZGWMXY3LU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016BayA4SZ2Cnj8CohGUxcUQ","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /work\nsed -i '' 's|triage/lead, triage/engineer, workers/engineer|triage/lead, triage/engineer, triage/product-manager, triage/architect, triage/designer, triage/documentation-planner, workers/engineer|' internal/roles/roles.go\npython3 - <<'EOF'\np='docs/proposal.md'\ns=open(p).read()\nm=\"The starter lead (`.ard/triage/lead/prompt.txt`) follows a fixed contract.\"\nadd=\"\"\"**Starter planning roles.** `ard init` also ships four planning roles, each writing its own `plan.md` section (`config.BuiltinPlanSections`) and its role file: `product-manager` (`## Requirements`: requirements, a numbered list of acceptance criteria, out of scope), `architect` (`## Design`: approach, affected modules, and an `ADR needed: yes|no` line; the worker writes any ADR in its pull request), `designer` (`## UX`, plus Markdown or script-free SVG files under `.ard/<issue#>/design/`) and `documentation-planner` (`## Docs`: which docs change and what each must say). The command line counts as a user interface, so the designer covers flags, output and messages. The starter ordering is product-manager, then architect; designer, then documentation-planner; the engineer runs after architect and documentation-planner (`after:` in the starter `config.yaml`). Note for #45: acceptance criteria are a numbered list under `### Acceptance criteria`.\n\n\"\"\"\nassert m in s\ns=s.replace(m,add+m,1)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngit -c core.excludesFile=/dev/null status --porcelain --untracked-files=all\ncat > .ard/40/worker-engineer.md <<'EOF'\n---\nrole: engineer\nstatus: done\nattempt: 1\n---\nAdds the four remaining starter triage roles (product-manager, architect, designer, documentation-planner) as embedded prompts with starter config and an `after:` ordering, so `ard init` ships a full triage set.\n\n## Changes\n- `internal/roles/triage/{product-manager,architect,designer,documentation-planner}/prompt.txt`: new prompts, each owning its built-in plan section (Requirements, Design, UX, Docs); the designer may also write `.ard/N/design/`.\n- `internal/roles/triage/lead/prompt.txt`: designer routing now includes command-line flags, output and messages.\n- `internal/roles/config.yaml`: overrides for the four roles; ordering product-manager, architect; designer, documentation-planner; engineer after architect and documentation-planner.\n- Tests: new `triage_roles_test.go` (load, model, `After`, section uniqueness, writable set, prompt shape, examples through `closeout.Parse` and `Build`); updated file lists in `roles_test.go` and `initcmd_test.go`; `engineer_test.go` expects the new `After`.\n- `docs/proposal.md`: describes the roles, the ordering and the acceptance-criteria shape for #45. `roles.go`: comment only.\n\n## Testing\nRan `go test ./internal/roles/... ./internal/initcmd/... ./internal/config/...`: all pass. `make test` was not run.\n\n## Open issues\n- `.ard/triage/` and `.ard/config.yaml` are not touched; copying the roles there for live sample runs is a human follow-up.\n- Design-file restrictions (no script, no external references) are enforced by the prompt only.\nEOF"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4527,"cache_read_input_tokens":34788,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4527},"output_tokens":42,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"287107ed-92e6-405f-9a57-346ff3681ee6","uuid":"63acadcd-21fc-493e-a930-b3d299b904e3","timestamp":"2026-11-23T21:12:39.398Z","request_id":"req_011ChLYnrKe6kVWv6HQhwKFH"}
